Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Give BowserBOYADVANCED a crisper 8-bit-style power-on sound.
Dependencies: Existing original startup chime and physical power lifecycle.

Purpose
-------
Replace the softer overlapping sine tones with a chip-style rising arpeggio
without changing the original melody, startup cue, mute/volume or game audio.

Tasks
-----
[x] Use square waves with shorter separated opening notes.
[x] Apply an eight-level decay,2ms attack and8ms final release.
[x] Preserve existing mute/volume, audio-context cleanup and permission errors.
[x] Add real rendered PCM and physical-power regressions without a supplied ROM.
[x] Finish focused validation.
[ ] Complete normal publication and verify the actual public startup.

Acceptance criteria
-------------------
Original three-note melody has a pulse-wave harmonic profile and crisp note
separation. Muted/zero volume creates no audio context; half volume halves
amplitude. No clipping, lingering tail, game-audio change or commercial sample.
Technical verification is not user listening approval.

Completion evidence
-------------------
The new PCM regression rejects old sine source, initially at its0.08946peak.
Original frequencies/start cue are retained. Syntax/build/all12units pass.
The new rendered-PCM/physical-power test, existing audio protection and startup
artwork tests pass3/3in13.2s. PCM checks cover strong square-wave third harmonic,
separated notes, bounded peak, exact half-volume ratio, mute/zero short-circuit,
silent tail and both context closures. Actual power switch creates3square
oscillators and completes startup without a cartridge.
The first final run passes PCM but times out because the fixture never picks
up the handheld before clicking its hidden power target. Add real pickup,
not forced interaction or a product change; the full affected group passes.
No listening/aesthetic approval is claimed.
No supplied demo ROM is executed.

